Usage: @CTL@ [options] command [arguments…]
Control the native WaylandShader GNOME extension over the session D-Bus.
Commands:
  status                         Print complete JSON status (does not load the effect)
  parameters                     Print declared parameters as JSON (does not load the effect)
  outputs                        Print connected monitors as JSON (does not load the effect)
  load FILE                      Load a .slangp preset and wait for compilation
  param NAME VALUE               Set a declared shader parameter
  output ID_OR_NAME shader on|off Enable/bypass the preset on one monitor
  output ID_OR_NAME color on|off  Enable/bypass color adjustments on one monitor
  output ID_OR_NAME gamma NUMBER  Set monitor gamma (0.1–5; 1 is neutral)
  output ID_OR_NAME saturation NUMBER
                                 Set monitor saturation (0–2; 1 is neutral)
  enable | disable               Set master desktop-effect enablement
  toggle                         Invert master desktop-effect enablement

Monitor selectors match an exact id first, otherwise a unique exact name.
Master disable bypasses both presets and color adjustments on all monitors.
Monitor controls preserve other settings and never enable the master switch.
Color adjustments work without a preset; shader and color switches are independent.
Mutation commands may enable only the waylandshader@man33li.github.com GNOME extension.
Exit codes: 0 success, 1 rejected/shader failure, 2 usage error,
3 unavailable/transport/protocol error, 4 timeout (operation may still finish).

Options:
  -h, --help           Displays help on commandline options.
  --help-all           Displays help, including generic Qt options.
  --timeout <seconds>  Overall deadline in seconds, including asynchronous
                       compilation (1–3600).

Arguments:
  command              One of the commands above.
  arguments            Command-specific arguments.
